.TH BOSWAS-PRESET 1 "October 2026" "boswas-branding 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-preset \- list and switch the Boswas OS desktop presets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B list
.br
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B current
.br
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B apply
.I PRESET
.RB [ \-\-layout ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Boswas OS ships ten presets of one design system: Horizon (the default),
Midnight, Aurora, Slate, Carbon, Pearl, Ocean, Ember, Nebula and Classic.
Each brings a Plasma Global Theme (colour scheme, Plasma style, icon theme,
window decoration), light, dark and lock-screen wallpapers, a panel layout
and a Konsole profile.
.PP
Boswas Control Center (Personalization) uses this command; the presets also
appear in System Settings > Global Theme.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
The presets with their identifier, name, description, light or dark variant
and accent colour, and the current preset.
.TP
.B current
The preset in use (the recorded choice, otherwise the active Global Theme).
.TP
.BI apply " PRESET"
Apply a preset for the signed-in user: Global Theme, desktop wallpaper,
lock-screen wallpaper and Konsole default profile. With
.BR \-\-layout ,
also replace the panels with the preset's layout (your own panel changes
are lost). Runs as the desktop user; refused for root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 a step failed (the message names it), 2 unknown preset,
3 usage error, 4 run as root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/boswas/presets/presets.json
The preset definitions.
.TP
.I ~/.config/boswasrc
The recorded choice ([Preset] Current).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-control-center (1)
